          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of William James</strong><br>\nWilliam James was born on January 11, 1842, in New York City to a wealthy family. His early education was varied and eccentric, involving tutors and private schools. Due to his family's wealth, James had the opportunity to travel to Europe and study in various institutions, receiving a broad education that included fine arts, science, and philosophy. This diverse educational background would later contribute to his versatile approaches in philosophy and psychology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Academic Journey</strong><br>\nJames initially studied painting before enrolling at Harvard University to study chemistry and then medicine. His wide array of interests led him to explore several subjects, contributing to his delay in settling on a career path. James did not receive his medical degree until 1869, demonstrating his reluctance to be rushed into a profession. His academic journey was characterized by curiosity and a drive to understand various human experiences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Principles of Psychology</strong><br>\nIn 1890, James published \"The Principles of Psychology,\" which became a seminal work in the field. The book explored the mind and consciousness from a practical perspective and was known for challenging existing psychological theories. James's work was significant for emphasizing the functions of consciousness and the ways it helps individuals adapt to their environments.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
